Implementation Plan - Completing and Polishing TravelGenie
This document outlines the proposed changes to complete TravelGenie and make it production-ready. We target critical backend anti-patterns (connection overhead, dynamic table updates, ML alphabetical bias, admin bypass) and frontend UI/UX polish (layouts, charts empty states, and auth state preservation).

User Review Required
IMPORTANT

Schema Baseline: All dynamic column alterations will be baselined in schema.sql. The runtime functions ensure_* will be converted to no-ops to eliminate table lock hazards.
ML Cost model: Replacing label-encoded LinearRegression (which uses alphabetical city indices to predict price) with a robust case-insensitive average city accommodation expense lookup table.
Database Connection Pool: Replacing connection-per-request with a thread-safe ThreadedConnectionPool from psycopg2.
Proposed Changes
Database Component
[MODIFY] 
db.py
Implement ThreadedConnectionPool using settings for database credentials.
Set pool boundaries (e.g., minimum 5, maximum 40 connections).
Create a PooledConnection wrapper class delegating method lookups via __getattr__ to the underlying connection, but overriding .close() to put the connection back in the pool (pool.putconn(conn)) instead of closing it physically.
Update get_connection() to return an instance of PooledConnection.
[MODIFY] 
schema.sql
Baseline the complete schema by defining all missing/runtime columns natively:
Add name VARCHAR(120) and is_deleted BOOLEAN DEFAULT FALSE directly to the users table definition.
Define the trips table which is missing but actively used by trips.py.
Baseline missing columns on the bookings table: package_title, package_image, travel_date, travelers, special_request, internal_notes, assigned_agent, adjusted_price.
Remove duplicate column alter definitions to keep the schema clean and maintainable.
Backend API Component
[MODIFY] 
admin.py
Make ensure_booking_workflow_columns and ensure_audit_tables no-ops.
Clean up connection calls ensuring that they release connections cleanly back to the pool.
[MODIFY] 
booking.py
Make ensure_booking_workflow_columns a no-op.
Validate incoming booking data correctly. Ensure it leverages pooled connections.
[MODIFY] 
auth.py
Make ensure_user_columns a no-op.
Modify save_user to insert the Firebase displayName into both name and full_name fields.
Update /login admin route to verify admin credentials against the admins table (with password hash verification) or fallback gracefully to environment variables (saving the username/password securely to the database upon first match).
